O6SJc60laRm","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T23:47:39Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T23:47:50Z","body":"I agree the temporary copies should be in `EditorPaths::get_temp_dir()` instead, unless there's a good reason for them to always be in the same folder.\n\ncc @dsnopek ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3029705830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032252769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108158#issuecomment-3032252769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108158","id":3032252769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60vIFh","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T13:22:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T13:22:23Z","body":"If I recall correctly the idea was so that any dependencies would still be able to be found? I'm not sure if this is the case (because I'm not a regular Windows user), but I think if your GDExtension depends on other DLLs, it'll find them in the same directory, which would mean that we'd need to know to copy the dependencies as well. I don't have a Windows machine available at the moment to test, but this would need to be confirmed\n\nAlso, some GDExtensions will use their library path (via `get_library_path` from the GDExtension interface) to find other associated files, although, I'm not sure if the library path will be the \"real\" path to the copy, or the original path. If that will always return the original path anyway, then that shouldn't matter","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032252769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033031044","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108158#issuecomment-3033031044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108158","id":3033031044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60yGGE","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T17:30:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T17:50:50Z","body":"> If I recall correctly the idea was so that any dependencies would still be able to be found?\n\nFrom the comments, that's correct.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/efb40c1524e54f2cf52f213e248bd0a7b790975a/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L477-L482\n\n> Also, some GDExtensions will use their library path (via `get_library_path` from the GDExtension interface) to find other associated files, although, I'm not sure if the library path will be the \"real\" path to the copy, or the original path. If that will always return the original path anyway, then that shouldn't matter\n\nI tested and `get_library_path` returns the path of the original file.\n\nIt is worth noting that we can't rely on presumed paths because the editor packs or copies files to different locations on export (DLLs are copied to the executable's root folder). I think that using `get_library_path` is required if the extension depends on the file path, and since it always returns the original path, the temporary copy could be placed in `.godot` without issues.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033031044/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033788656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108158#issuecomment-3033788656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108158","id":3033788656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc600_Dw","user":{"login":"sinni800","id":2879097,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzkwOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2879097?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800","html_url":"https://github.com/sinni800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T21:59:35Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T22:05:01Z","body":"Also in addition to that, if we try to script exports by running another copy of the engine (it seems we can't run a full export with gdscript from within the engine right now?), it will create another copy with .TMP at the end and then never delete it. It leaves a lot of temp files after a while...\n\nMaybe if this tilde copy already exists, just load that one (if possible, and if not, create another copy)\n\nA workaround for my use case, if you don't need the GDExtensions for exporting, --recovery-mode will not load these but still properly export. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033788656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]